  "difficulty_reason": "The selected theorem requires uniform control across conjugacy classes whose small-cycle parameters can vary with n, rather than a fixed-distribution Poisson limit. The authors first establish three-regime common-invariant-set bounds and uniform orbit tails, then derive mixed factorial-moment errors using optimized cycle cutoffs and handle a degenerating-parameter alternative when applying Bonferroni truncation. This source-local uniform sparse-orbit approximation with coupled parameter regimes is substantially beyond ordinary doctoral qualification probability exercises.",
